{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison","id":1383253,"title":"The Element(s) of Poison","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-22T17:52:17-07:00","id":1383253,"title":"The Element(s) of Poison","content":"I was thinking about <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F0l6dr49MG0\" target=\"_blank\">mid-season episodes of Dr. Stone</a> a day or two ago and, while reading the Wood Aspect anima power again (post 1e, of course), it struck me as odd that Wood is the only element associated with poisonous substances. While plant life certainly gets by on using them as a defense through a lot of different flora, Creation presumably has lots of volcanoes, springs, and other sites of harsh geology that give off toxic gases. Lookshy, as of the pdf expansion preview, even pulls a Delphic Oracle bit with a less toxic example of this concept (one sorcerous ritual relies on what is ethylene gas, to us, making the sorcerer goofy and giggly for a bit, like alcohol consumption). The Mountain Folk Storytelling chapter for 2e even acknowledged the hazards of spelunking with dangerous gases that lurk below the ground. I feel that this is very much underplayed for non-Wood Aspects, while Wood probably dwells a bit too much on amygdalin and plants like the Manchineel.<br /> <br /> It's not like this is a subtle, little-known and obscure danger, either. Volcanoes and geysers and rather loud and noticeable when active; they'll also stink and make bystanders gag on sulfur fumes. Any body of water near a volcano is liable to kill those nearby en masse, too; if there's a god present and of sufficient ambition, they might even advertise this fact, and garner worship by threatening to make the problem creep down further than it usually does, or release all of the &quot;quiet gas&quot; in the lake all at once. By all rights, a toxic anima effect ought to be common among every Aspect but Air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T23:43:34-07:00","id":1383299,"title":"","content":"&gt;Makes apost about toxic <i>gas</i><br /> &gt;Says Air shouldn't get that power<br /> <br /> I think you could fit poison themes to any Aspect. But it's not just poison.<br /> <br /> The Earth Anima can knock people prone. Can vines not trip people? Can wind and wave not knock someone down?<br /> <br /> If you want to expand poison, make a Charm for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:13:34-07:00","id":1383313,"title":"","content":"This is a fine point to make for elemental spirits, but I think in a majority of respects the distinctions in Dragon Blooded Aspects should prioritise the distinction in character types and gameplay modes rather through its delineations, rather than look for every possible thing each element can act as an umbrella for.<br /> <br /> In design and in-character these Exalted function in terms of an interdependent pattern.<br /> <br /> I think it helps to think of their elements specifically in terms of a particular iconic quality for this group of people, rather than the Dragon Blooded fully embodying everything iconic to each element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:25:53-07:00","id":1383316,"title":"","content":"A long time ago I was tinkering with the idea of new elements made by combining two base elements (based on something I saw watching an episode of naruto late at night when nothing else was on). Came up with poison being the combination of Wood+Water. <br /> <br /> Lame idea ultimatly, bit I do think it is under more than just wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T02:51:28-07:00","id":1383318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383313#post1383313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a fine point to make for elemental spirits, but I think in a majority of respects the distinctions in Dragon Blooded Aspects should prioritise the distinction in character types and gameplay modes rather through its delineations, rather than look for every possible thing each element can act as an umbrella for.<br /> <br /> In design and in-character these Exalted function in terms of an interdependent pattern.<br /> <br /> I think it helps to think of their elements specifically in terms of a particular iconic quality for this group of people, rather than the Dragon Blooded fully embodying everything iconic to each element.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Isator.<br /> <br /> It's not always easy to delineate the themes of the Aspects, but it is kind of important. You could of course have them all using similar powers with just different visual themes (and there are a few charms like that, ie attack with your element, but they do tend to at least have small differences: fire bolts do slightly more damage, while water bolts can flow around shields and lightning bolts get bonuses vs metal armour).<br /> But I think that would in reality make Dragonblood more boring.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also... in terms of combat specifically, I think Wood sometimes suffers a bit. Earth is about being super-tough, Fire is about doing more damage, Air is about ranged stuff, Water's all flowy and dodgy and Kung-Fu*. They have done a bit with Wood and Stamina this edition (hence why my Wood Aspect archer has Strength 4, Dexterity 4 and Stamina 5... what kind of other archer would have Stamina as their top attribute?), but giving them poison is a big deal, combat-wise.** Without it, I can really see Wood Aspects feeling like they're the poor man of Dragonblood combat characters. And unlike Solars, the intention with Dragonblood is that one Aspect is the non-combat social aspect.<br /> <br /> *Kung-Fu is such a big part of Exalted that being slightly more about Kung-Fu than all the other Kung-Fu heroes is pretty significant.<br /> <br /> **Despite saying this, my 300xp Wood Aspect doesn't have any charms that inflict poison. He's got a few workhorse and anti-undead archery and occult charms, and a ton of Resistance charms. I actually don't like using poison much, as I find it yet another thing to keep track of in combat, plus it's often not all that great. But for really difficult fights, when I'm flaring, then anyone who takes anima damage takes a difficulty 9 poison hit, and I took Poisoner's Deft Hand since it has few prereqs, so I can boost that to difficulty <i>11</i>. Now that's serious poison, even if it's only 2i a round/-1. The kind that makes people throw down big fat Resistance excellencies (if they can).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:56:01-07:00","id":1383341,"title":"","content":"I disagree with Isator.<br /> <br /> Air is all about Thrown. But you should be able to play an Air swordsman if you like.<br /> <br /> There's a Fire Charm that boosts your Appearance for a roll. There's a Wood Charm that boosts your Appearance for the duration of your Aura state.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for the different elements to achieve the same thing in different ways.<br /> <br /> But the default presentation is the default.<br /> <br /> If your Dragon-Blooded is a scholastic Air eunch who poisons his enemies, I think that should be viable character space. I don't think the devs should publish a rafter of Air Aspect poison Charms, but I do think that there is design space for custom Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T07:17:14-07:00","id":1383360,"title":"","content":"Fakharu has Seven Venoms Exhalation, and he's a water dragon, after all. Clearly wood doesn't have a monopoly.<br /> <br /> If I could actually think of five different interesting, thematic, and mostly-balanced poison effects, I'd be all in favor of nasty poison tricks for every element. Hell, create a Charm called Venom of the Five Dragons with five elemental variants like Elemental Bolt Attack.<br /> <br /> (I was recently trying to think of decent Charm ideas for Solar poisoners. I should give that some more consideration.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:09:48-07:00","id":1383416,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11237\" data-vbnamecard=\"11237\">Jefepato</a> In 1e, there was a Lore Charm that could turn water into a poison just by applying heat for an extended period of time. It was in the Night book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383299#post1383299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Makes apost about toxic <i>gas</i><br /> &gt;Says Air shouldn't get that power<br /> <br /> I think you could fit poison themes to any Aspect. But it's not just poison.<br /> <br /> The Earth Anima can knock people prone. Can vines not trip people? Can wind and wave not knock someone down?<br /> <br /> If you want to expand poison, make a Charm for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was in the process of that, but my homebrew capacity has been broken for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T16:43:08-07:00","id":1383469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383416#post1383416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11237_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11237\" data-vbnamecard=\"11237\">Jefepato</a> In 1e, there was a Lore Charm that could turn water into a poison just by applying heat for an extended period of time. It was in the Night book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but I'm familiar with that one and I'm not really a fan. &quot;Boil water and transmute it into poison&quot; doesn't IMO make a lot of sense as a Solar Charm (sounds more like sorcery, or possibly thaumaturgy). A Solar brewing or distilling poison should use <i>some</i> kind of ingredients, even if they're not something a mortal brewer could have turned into an effective poison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T18:56:13-07:00","id":1383495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383341#post1383341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the devs should publish a rafter of Air Aspect poison Charms, but I do think that there is design space for custom Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that statement applies to a lot of Exalted. There's lots of charms that could exist but probably shouldn't be published because for one, the books would be so bloated omg, and for another it helps keep some identity and iconic abilities. Like the Dragonblooded ability to shoot arrows out of the sky with their own arrows, or the Solar ability to do...something particular to only Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T23:34:25-07:00","id":1383520,"title":"","content":"It doesn't get shilled as much as Wood by the game, but Water did get a poison association in Ex2 with Craft (Water) being the one to use when making poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T02:02:29-07:00","id":1383535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383341#post1383341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Air is all about Thrown. But you should be able to play an Air swordsman if you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>In bits and pieces, but it seems apparent that Dragon Blooded Charm technology ultimately comes down against the idea that the complication of balancing different elements can be overcome by substituting elements in Abilities entirely.<br /> <br /> An Air Aspect can include some sword fighting in their repertoire of Air-based fighting techniques. The Air Aspect who is dedicated specifically to being a sword fighter needs to learn to manage the Fire Element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Fire Charm that boosts your Appearance for a roll. There's a Wood Charm that boosts your Appearance for the duration of your Aura state.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of room for the different elements to achieve the same thing in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find poison in this context to qualify as a way rather than a thing.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly talking about something like how Water gets the characterisation as having the sneaky, underhanded, even cruel methods. A person might make an argument for any of those qualities in the iconography of the other elements, but they ultimately go to Water, one part of a wider purpose of creating deeper distinctions in character and interdependence between abilities.<br /> <br /> Poison here gets to be part of Wood's purview of interaction with the vital tissues, to harm or to heal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the devs should publish a rafter of Air Aspect poison Charms, but I do think that there is design space for custom Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but I'm addressing the statement about what the Dragon Blooded &quot;ought&quot; to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T02:28:35-07:00","id":1383540,"title":"","content":"True for sure, however I think it's more about delineating what we feel the &quot;mythic essence&quot; of what each element is about. We could similarly make a case that Solars should have poison magic through essence infusion as well as through skill, because sunstroke is a sort of poisoning... but that wouldn't really fit with the mythic essence of the sun as the setting develops it. It's like that with the other elements than Wood; biology is not really their essential province.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T03:48:54-07:00","id":1383547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383535#post1383535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In bits and pieces, but it seems apparent that Dragon Blooded Charm technology ultimately comes down against the idea that the complication of balancing different elements can be overcome by substituting elements in Abilities entirely.<br /> <br /> An Air Aspect can include some sword fighting in their repertoire of Air-based fighting techniques. The Air Aspect who is dedicated specifically to being a sword fighter needs to learn to manage the Fire Element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm.... I think, while some elements are stronger in certain abilities than others, there's still an aim to make it valid to use any ability with any Aspect, and do things a different way.<br /> So a Fire Aspect swordsman blinds their opponent and does more damage, an Air Aspect takes careful aim before lethal strikes, a Water Aspect uses a flowing defence, etc. But general &quot;just be accurate&quot; is balanced.<br /> Similarly an Air Aspect throws arcing daggers that are more accurate against people in armour, an Earth Aspect throws them harder to knock people over, a Fire Aspect throws them and they explode.<br /> My Wood Aspect has a ton of Resistance, he's extremely tough, but at no point will this ever require him to drop out of Wood Aura if he doesn't want to. I was thinking about playing an Earth Aspect and using Brawl; they're not as good in some ways as a Water Aspect, but they're skilled at just punching people really hard and knocking them to the ground.<br /> <br /> But saying that...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find poison in this context to qualify as a way rather than a thing. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. There's a fair few combat abilities where Wood's way of doing that combat ability is just &quot;you can inflict poison&quot; (which combos well with Medicine). If you could do that with other abilities, then Wood would have no special or distinct way of fighting across the different combat abilities.<br /> I guess it'd be the same as if you made a bunch of Air charms for knocking people back or over (which could make sense, you push them with wind), at that point there's nothing distinct about the way that Earth uses combat abilities.<br /> <br /> (Saying this, <i>resisting</i> poison does literally have a Water and Air charm. Because it's poison-related, but it's not a way of using a combat ability.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's more about delineating what we feel the &quot;mythic essence&quot; of what each element is about... It's like that with the other elements than Wood; biology is not really their essential province. </div> </div> </div>This too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:55:55-07:00","id":1383563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383547#post1383547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm.... I think, while some elements are stronger in certain abilities than others, there's still an aim to make it valid to use any ability with any Aspect, and do things a different way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use any Ability, but those Abilities still come with conditions for how they're used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Fire Aspect swordsman blinds their opponent and does more damage, an Air Aspect takes careful aim before lethal strikes</div> </div> </div> </div>When Heirs to the Shogunate comes out in a form I can read, am I going to find a bunch of additional Air Melee Charms, or will they still have only two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:16:38-07:00","id":1383571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383563#post1383563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When Heirs to the Shogunate comes out in a form I can read, am I going to find a bunch of additional Air Melee Charms, or will they still have only two?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:19:15-07:00","id":1383572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383563#post1383563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When Heirs to the Shogunate comes out in a form I can read, am I going to find a bunch of additional Air Melee Charms, or will they still have only two?</div> </div> </div> </div>4 new air-aspected melee charms currently in Heirs, building off aiming (i.e. focusing on one particular approach to melee), plus another defensive melee charm that has different versions for each aspect (a la Dragon-Graced Weapon).<br /> <br /> For sake of completeness, WFHW has 2 solely air-aspected melee charms, Elemental Sheath and Dragon-Graced Weapon (air functionality/variants) and 6 balanced melee charms (just counted...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":".  Forgot one of the charms in Heirs didn't I...? 04-24-2020, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T06:45:41-07:00","id":1383590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383535#post1383535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find poison in this context to qualify as a way rather than a thing.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly talking about something like how Water gets the characterisation as having the sneaky, underhanded, even cruel methods. A person might make an argument for any of those qualities in the iconography of the other elements, but they ultimately go to Water, one part of a wider purpose of creating deeper distinctions in character and interdependence between abilities.<br /> <br /> Poison here gets to be part of Wood's purview of interaction with the vital tissues, to harm or to heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, disagree.<br /> <br /> Poison is a sneaky, underhanded, perhaps cruel means. Poison is not a way.<br /> <br /> Healing or harming the body is the Wood way. And poison is a definite part of that.<br /> <br /> But it's a means, not a method. It thematically fits just as well within Water's purview of being indirect. (As well as the elemental/chemical associations expressed in the OP.)<br /> <br /> Disengaging is Fire Aspected with Heat-of-Battle Advance. It's Water Aspected with Ebbing Tide Receeds (which has HoBA as a prereq). Loads of DB Charms work along refining elemental themes (Warm Faced Seduction Style into Vivacious Dragon Beauty) or expressing similiar ends with different elements (another Dodge example is Air Aspected Safety Among Enemies and Air/Water Aspected Heart Like Water).<br /> <br /> I think taking a Wood Aspected poison Charm then adding a Earth Aspected Charm to that tree to expresses poison through a different elemental lens is exactly what you should be doing with DB custom Charms.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. &quot;I'm playing an Earth Aspect but don't want to deal with Aura so this Wood Charm is now Earth&quot; is something I'm absolutely against. You can't just say &quot;Earth is poisonous so I get poison powers now&quot;. You have to refine the Charm an express it through the element, as Exalted defines the elements.<br /> <br /> But Wood doesn't get a monopoly on poison just because it's Wood.<br /> <br /> Because of its themes (as Exalted defines them), poison/venom fits <i>naturally</i> under Wood. It defaults to Wood. It's not exclusive to Wood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-24-2020, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T18:13:34-07:00","id":1383701,"title":"","content":"In 1e, there was no hide or hair of Wood being the poison aspect. In fact, there weren't really many, if any, poison effects at all for Dragon-Blooded in 1e. 2e leaned hard into making Wood Aspects out to be Poison Ivy, possibly to make them seem like awful hypocrites if they followed the Immaculate Philosophy, which eschews the use of poison because it allows lessers to usurp their betters. That, of course, sets up the obvious dig on the Immaculates for supporting the present position, which was likely achieved with some poison use against the Solars...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383469#post1383469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, but I'm familiar with that one and I'm not really a fan. &quot;Boil water and transmute it into poison&quot; doesn't IMO make a lot of sense as a Solar Charm (sounds more like sorcery, or possibly thaumaturgy). A Solar brewing or distilling poison should use <i>some</i> kind of ingredients, even if they're not something a mortal brewer could have turned into an effective poison.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could add a fact introduction action regarding compounds that a character collected to replace the out of place meditation action. The rest of the mechanics seem like they might not need much changing, though perhaps instead of setting poison variables at trait ratings, the fact reflects various benchmarks in comparison with other poisons. You could also make the spontaneous weapon-coating Charm an after the fact declaration with sufficient successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T20:09:12-07:00","id":1383711,"title":"","content":"To my way of thinking, <i>geology</i> isn't the same thing as <i>Earth</i>. The examples in the OP feel like what in Creation would be manifestations of corrupted or imbalanced essence (the kind of thing that spawns elementals to correct it) rather than anything to do with &quot;pure&quot; Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T21:02:32-07:00","id":1383715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383711#post1383711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my way of thinking, <i>geology</i> isn't the same thing as <i>Earth</i>. The examples in the OP feel like what in Creation would be manifestations of corrupted or imbalanced essence (the kind of thing that spawns elementals to correct it) rather than anything to do with &quot;pure&quot; Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use of the term &quot;corrupted&quot; with regard to Essence is rather curious, seeing as how that term typically describes something from outside of Creation, which presumably doesn't include volcanic processes. Also, &quot;pure&quot; elemental manifestations only really happen at the poles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T21:58:38-07:00","id":1383718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383701#post1383701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could add a fact introduction action regarding compounds that a character collected to replace the out of place meditation action. The rest of the mechanics seem like they might not need much changing, though perhaps instead of setting poison variables at trait ratings, the fact reflects various benchmarks in comparison with other poisons. You could also make the spontaneous weapon-coating Charm an after the fact declaration with sufficient successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I was planning to entirely ignore the Charms in CB: Night and just write new Charms, but what you just described is a lot like what I had in mind anyway.<br /> <br /> The simplest possible idea would be something similar to the DB Charm Poisoner's Deft Hand, just...Solar-level.<br /> <br /> Another idea would be a Craft or Medicine Charm wherein the Solar distills a superior poison, by picking an existing poison (from the standard list or from some venomous animal's statblock or whatever) and improving it somehow. Or by improvising ingredients (insert fact introduction and/or Survival check here) to end up making something equivalent.<br /> <br /> (My concern is that if &quot;brew an awesome poison&quot; and &quot;deliver poison especially well&quot; Charms both exist, using them together could get out of hand.)<br /> <br /> As for spontaneous weapon-coating...I guess it's not unreasonable to have a Charm that lets the Solar's player retroactively declare &quot;I poisoned my dagger earlier!&quot; but it probably makes just as much sense to have a Charm that lets the Solar reflexively apply the poison as they attack. (Lunars can already do pretty much exactly this with Adder Fang Method as long as they stunt.) Of course, there's always that Craft Charm in MotSE for retroactively having finished a project, which could be a lot of fun for a Solar chemist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T22:18:52-07:00","id":1383720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383715#post1383715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use of the term &quot;corrupted&quot; with regard to Essence is rather curious, seeing as how that term typically describes something from outside of Creation\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it?<br /> <br /> Demesnes are a feature of Creation, and yet their turbulent Essence can twist and mutate the beings living there. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t find it unreasonable to refer to a group of humans who have spent years living in an earth-aspected cave demesne, with the word \u201ccorrupted.\u201d Earth Essence has deprived them of eyesight and given them snake tongues that let them sense body heat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-25-2020, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T23:54:56-07:00","id":1383726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383720#post1383720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it?<br /> <br /> Demesnes are a feature of Creation, and yet their turbulent Essence can twist and mutate the beings living there.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t find it unreasonable to refer to a group of humans who have spent years living in an earth-aspected cave demesne, with the word \u201ccorrupted.\u201d Earth Essence has deprived them of eyesight and given them snake tongues that let them sense body heat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gem Lords send their lackeys out to secure sites like those. So unless all of those are supposed to be metaphysically corrupted (as opposed to ethically corrupted, which I suspect they all are, yeah), I don't think that it applies as a thing, no. It's perfectly fine Earth Essence, as experienced by Earth elementals and other beings of similar stature or greater. If mortals can't channel Essence... that's bad for them, but says nothing about the Essence if everything is going to have a similar reaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T00:30:49-07:00","id":1383730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383726#post1383726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gem Lords send their lackeys out to secure sites like those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that <i>every</i> earth aspected demesne is accounted for thusly, then? <br /> <br /> If not, then my example still works.<br /> <br /> And if so\u2026 okay, swap \u201cearth\u201d for \u201cwood\u201d and substitute other appropriate mutations, and my point still stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383726#post1383726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So unless all of those are supposed to be metaphysically corrupted (as opposed to ethically corrupted, which I suspect they all are, yeah), I don't think that it applies as a thing, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not talking about the demesnes - I\u2019m talking about the humans. <br /> <br /> How is being suffused enough with an energy or substance that it changes your physical form in a deleterious way <i>not</i> corruption?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T03:15:08-07:00","id":1383744,"title":"","content":"The setting has generally included instances where Creation's natural processes can acquire errors or breakdowns that mess them up in a manner that could be described as a corruption. Watching out for that kind of thing is part of what gods and Sidereals do.<br /> <br /> The assertion that things such as the harmful side effects of many natural processes constitutes a form of corruption is patently absurd. This isn't Lord of the Rings, a swamp is not a manifestation of evil because it has features that are aesthetically unpleasing or physically harmful to humans, those things actually contribute to it being a vital and thriving ecosystem in its own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T09:12:25-07:00","id":1383780,"title":"","content":"&quot;Corrupted&quot; was a bad word choice on my part; connotations are too judgemental. I should have said something like &quot;unstable&quot;, &quot;irregular&quot;, or &quot;unsettled&quot;.<br /> <br /> My point was that the metaphysical space, the... &quot;ground state&quot; if you will, of the Earth Element doesn't have to extend to cover everything modern science would call &quot;geology&quot;. Some minerals and underground gasses are toxic, but that doesn't mean that &quot;toxicity&quot; is associated with Elemental Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-25-2020, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T15:19:10-07:00","id":1383851,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, if the earth should contain toxins, that is perhaps not an expression, necessarily of Earth Essence being true to its essential (or &quot;Platonic&quot;) nature. It's perhaps an expression of mixtures of essence (Wood aspected, Death aspected, etc.).<br /> <br /> (And here is where we may, or may not, segue onto discussing whether this conflicts with how much Creation does or does not have what we'd recognize as chemistry, and folk who wonder how important this is for what Exalted is about give me a hard stare).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T19:35:31-07:00","id":1383895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383851#post1383851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean, if the earth should contain toxins, that is perhaps not an expression, necessarily of Earth Essence being true to its essential (or &amp;quot;Platonic&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> nature. It's perhaps an expression of mixtures of essence (Wood aspected, Death aspected, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or insufficient essence; maybe not enough stabilizing Earth essence reached a given formation. Or it pooled for a while before being cutoff and thus stagnated. OR, maybe it's the result of some completely different natural process. Not everything has to be the result of Dragon Lines intersecting or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T00:10:36-07:00","id":1383917,"title":"","content":"While one could no doubt point out more than one that I made in the thread, gunning for Earth was a goof. The conversation is apparently about Fire now, according to a forgetfully-delayed check on Old MacDonald's Codex, though Earth is associated with lead, according to the same, and mineral toxins like arsenic assuredly don't have anything to do with Wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T03:15:30-07:00","id":1383928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383851#post1383851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean, if the earth should contain toxins, that is perhaps not an expression, necessarily of Earth Essence being true to its essential (or &amp;quot;Platonic&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find little to nothing to be Platonic in the cosmology of the setting.<br /> <br /> The question depends on whether or not one sees each Element as a singularity or an umbrella, and considering things like the large lost of correspondences given to them for the sake of things like manses and demesnes and the large range of types for each elemental, I see it more as the latter.<br /> <br /> I mean, I have a personal bias against Platonism, it just happens to be consistent with how the books have generally portrayed things.<br /> <br /> That is a separate matter from the Dragon Blooded though; they're not personifications of the elements, they're just one more thing hanging out under the umbrella.<br /> <br /> (I find the argument that relates poison to the thematic purpose of Dragon Blooded Water to be far more credible. It's not quite for me, but it's at least going along with what I understand of the Dragon Blooded rules.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T03:17:22-07:00","id":1383929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383917#post1383917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mineral toxins like arsenic assuredly don't have anything to do with Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody look at why we named the metal cobalt after the sprite from Germanic folklore, and tell me if would not be an Earth Elemental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T04:09:18-07:00","id":1383937,"title":"","content":"I think you may be over-interpreting that scare-quote a little. On commenting on your post content I certainly think they're closer to a &quot;singularity&quot; than &quot;am umbrella which encompasses any complex phenomena which we can notionally associate with an element&quot; (which leads to &quot;Ice is water and therefore there should be Resistance Charms around being hard like ice&quot; and thereby lies an approach to Dragon-blooded and more broadly on elemental magic on which I am not keen - elements and elemental magic should be simple, finite, well characterised and non-overlapping, ideally as much as possible). Though perhaps maybe it could be closer to an umbrella of narrow form. I will avoid getting into any furter Deled-esque arguments about the nature of elements and essence within the world, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:19:36-07:00","id":1384072,"title":"","content":"Even if you're just arguing the list of concepts associated with an element, well, again, Earth includes lead. That implies that in addition to being heavy, it can also be deceptively toxic while appearing easy to work with. Fire, meanwhile, can turn even relatively benign Earth or Wood into a choking blanket of smoke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383929#post1383929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somebody look at why we named the metal cobalt after the sprite from Germanic folklore, and tell me if would not be an Earth Elemental.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, the mine-dwelling kobold. Now, if you'll excuse me, I'll go have a laugh at yet another arsenic species in the form of the molecular formula for cobaltite (the other juvenile giggle-worthy one being the semi-aromatic ring structure known as arsole).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T00:08:59-07:00","id":1384115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1383937#post1383937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you may be over-interpreting that scare-quote a little. On commenting on your post content I certainly think they're closer to a &quot;singularity&quot; than &quot;am umbrella which encompasses any complex phenomena which we can notionally associate with an element&quot; (which leads to &quot;Ice is water and therefore there should be Resistance Charms around being hard like ice&quot; and thereby lies an approach to Dragon-blooded and more broadly on elemental magic on which I am not keen - elements and elemental magic should be simple, finite, well characterised and non-overlapping, ideally as much as possible). Though perhaps maybe it could be closer to an umbrella of narrow form. I will avoid getting into any furter Deled-esque arguments about the nature of elements and essence within the world, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Dragon-Blooded Charms are an umbrella.<br /> <br /> Dodge is Fire. Except when you drift away like Air, or flow away like Water, or you sway like grass then it's Wood, or you stand perfectly still and cause an earthquake with Earth.<br /> <br /> But that's not all. Air can redirect attacks coming at you. Wood can leap you in the way of your allies. Water can knock your enemies off balance. Earth can blind your enemies. Fire increases your damage (in <i>Dodge</i>).<br /> <br /> Then we look at Melee where it's Fire that blinds enemies and leaps you in front of your allies, Earth which knocks them prone, Wood increases your damage, Water embodies steam in a Clash Charm (&quot;Water vapor or rain boils into steam as the arc of the Dragon-Blood\u2019s attack agitates them with ferocious Essence, whipping a great cloud from the air as she intercepts her enemy\u2019s blow&quot;). Air gives multiple attacks. Fire gives multiple attacks. Water gives multiple attacks.<br /> <br /> More generally, Air can blast people with wind, freeze them in ice or zap them with lightning.<br /> <br /> These aren't obscure, backer-only, homebrew Charms. These are the core, canon Charms in What Fire Has Wrought.<br /> <br /> Blinding Spark Distraction blinds enemies with sparks from weapons hitting each other. Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion blinds enemies by throwing dirt in their eyes. One Charm is Fire. One is Earth. Fire isn't the element of blinding people. Dragon-Blooded blind people with their supra-human skill, and they express that skill through the element of Fire. Or Earth. Both elements achieve the same result, but they do it in different ways. You can't just take Blinding Spark Distraction and say &quot;this is Earth now&quot;, but you can add a custom Charm with Blinding Spark Distraction as a prereq to blind enemies with a Reflexive/Counter-Attack mudslinging Gambit.<br /> <br /> A Resistance Charm that makes one hard like ice is completely apropos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-27-2020, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T06:53:08-07:00","id":1384182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1384115#post1384115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Resistance Charm that makes one hard like ice is completely apropos.</div> </div> </div> </div>But would it necessarily be in Resistance? If Fire blinds enemies in Melee and Earth blinds enemies in Dodge, maybe Water can harden to ice somewhere other than Resistance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T07:07:14-07:00","id":1384184,"title":"","content":"Nah, because it's hardening to ice to make you tougher.<br /> <br /> If it was hardening your fists to ice to punch people for more damage, it wouldn't be Resistance of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T10:33:23-07:00","id":1384218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1384182#post1384182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But would it necessarily be in Resistance? If Fire blinds enemies in Melee and Earth blinds enemies in Dodge, maybe Water can harden to ice somewhere other than Resistance?</div> </div> </div> </div>It naturally fits in Resistance.<br /> <br /> But as there's a Fire Charm that blinds in Thrown (putting blinding in Dodge, Melee and Thrown), I could see a &quot;Body of Water and Ice&quot; Air/Water Dodge Charm which makes you tougher when you avoid an attack. Or a Survival Charm for enduring hot terrain by cladding you in Ice Armor (which also makes you tougher). Or an Integrity Charm that freezes your heart (the head can be pursauded) and turns you into a living statue of ice.<br /> <br /> The important thing to remember is that Dragon-Blooded are not Element Based Exalted. They're Ability Based Exalts.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Charms are supra-natural skill, reflected through the elemental associations of Creation.<br /> <br /> If the main purpose of the Charm is to make you tougher, by invoking the elemental associations of &quot;ice&quot; (which fits under both Water and Air) then the &quot;main purpose&quot; part trumps the &quot;elemental associations&quot; part. Becoming tougher is a Resistance thing. Why would you want that some place other than Resistance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:06:47-07:00","id":1384223,"title":"","content":"John, I am at odds with those sort of presentations of how Dragonblooded elemental magic works, where any element is sort of SFX to unlocks anything you want (like &quot;My resistance Charms are hardened lava, summoned by the element of Fire&quot; and suchlike). Narrower &quot;umbrellas&quot; are better.<br /> <br /> But I feel like that's a conversation direction that will set me at odds with most Exalted-likers, who from experience are probably more inclined to defend a more &quot;Whatever-you-want&quot; school of elemental magic (than a &quot;Each element has defined un-surpassable strengths and weaknesses for the Dragonblooded; work with it, not against it&quot;), and probably at odds with the edition drift, so it's not too much worth pursuing further (as it feels it will go towards one of those many-on-one sort of conversations that results mainly in dug in heels and doesn't really result in anyone doing or saying anything fun or creative)...<br /> <br /> In terms of the thread topic, I do think that modes like a lack of directly poisonous magic under other elements are a vestige of narrower umbrellas (and a good thing), and towards more of a tendency to see complex elemental phenomena as due to combinations of essence than as purely driven by elemental essence (which I also prefer in the metaphysics - ice is water+air+earth, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:30:04-07:00","id":1384229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383253-the-element-s-of-poison?p=1384223#post1384223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">John, I am at odds with those sort of presentations of how Dragonblooded elemental magic works, where any element is sort of SFX to unlocks anything you want (like &amp;quot;My resistance Charms are hardened lava, summoned by the element of Fire&amp;quot; and suchlike). Narrower &amp;quot;umbrellas&amp;quot; are better.<br /> <br /> But I feel like that's a conversation direction that will set me at odds with most Exalted-likers, who from experience are probably more inclined to defend a more &amp;quot;Whatever-you-want&amp;quot; school of elemental magic (than a &amp;quot;Each element has defined un-surpassable strengths and weaknesses for the Dragonblooded; work with it, not against it&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, and probably at odds with the edition drift, so it's not too much worth pursuing further (as it feels it will go towards one of those many-on-one sort of conversations that results mainly in dug in heels and doesn't really result in anyone doing or saying anything fun or creative)...</div> </div> </div> </div>We disagree, but not as far as you might seem.<br /> <br /> I have nothing against an Air Charm making you tougher like Ice. But it shouldn't be better than an Earth Charm that makes you tougher. And it shouldn't be a straight port of an Earth Charm.<br /> <br /> In 2E there was a Charm that made you tougher based on your armor. Jade was better than metal. White Jade was better than any other color. But you could still make your fiery Red Jade armor tougher.<br /> <br /> I don't like locking character concepts behind element walls. Tepet Arada should be playable, and saying &quot;All Melee Charms are Fire&quot; is diametrically against that. <br /> <br /> That said the elements should be discreet. Tepet Arada and Cathak Cainan should not have the same fighting style but one in Blue and one in Red.<br /> <br /> Air Melee and Fire Melee, RAW are distinct. And I enjoy that distinction.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean that just because Air has a multiple attack Charm that Fire shouldn't have one. Instead they should evoke different themes, and both need to be naturally grounded in their Charm cascades.<br /> <br /> If you're saying &quot;only Fire Aspects get to use swords, Air has to use Chakrams&quot;, then you are right -- there's no sense continuing this conversation.<br /> <br /> If you're saying &quot;Fire should be the best with swords&quot;, we disagree but I'll meet you in the middle.<br /> <br /> I'm saying &quot;Both Fire and Air should be able to use swords. Because swords are Melee -- not an element.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}